  "notes": "Census from the vendor tech-spec table (https://techspecs.ui.com/uisp/wired/es-16-150w, HTTP 200, 574,980 B, read 2026-11-20): Networking interface \"(16) 10/100/1000 Mbps RJ45 ports; (2) 1 Gbps SFP ports\"; PoE interface \"PoE/PoE+ (Pins 1, 2+; 3, 6-); 24V DC passive PoE (Pins 4, 5+; 7, 8-)\"; max per port \"PoE+: 34.2W; Passive PoE: 17W\"; management \"UART console Out-of-Band\". The 16 copper ports were declared 1G/100M although the page states 10/100/1000 Mbps - the 10M rung is now modelled, matching the same fix PR #2249 made across the ECS family. Budget note: this page prints \"Power supply: AC/DC, internal, 150W\" and \"Max. power consumption: 150W\" and no \"Total PoE available\" row, so the 150 W here is still the SKU-named figure and has not been re-sourced by this pass."
